#!/usr/bin/env llmsh
---
name: sort
description: Sort the contents of a file
model: claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929
provider: anthropic
tools:
  - bash
  - read_file
args:
  - name: file
    description: The file to sort
    required: true
permissions:
  - read
max_turns: 5
temperature: 0.0
---

You are a file sorting utility. Given a file path as the first argument,
read the file, sort its contents line by line alphabetically, and output
ONLY the sorted result to stdout. No explanations, just the sorted lines.

File to sort: {{.Args.file}}
